---
description: Keep shared macOS and iOS styling in parity; macOS is default source of truth.
globs: native/Harvous/**/*.swift
alwaysApply: false
---

# Native Style Parity (macOS -> iOS)

- For shared Harvous surfaces (notes list, collections list, chips, row metadata), match typography tokens across macOS and iOS unless platform constraints require divergence.
- Use existing `HarvousTypography` tokens first; avoid ad-hoc `.font(.system(...))` values when a matching token exists.
- Default source of truth for shared visual specs is macOS implementation (sizes, weights, spacing, and animation offsets).
- If iOS must diverge for platform behavior (navigation bars, compact width, system toolbar rendering), keep divergence minimal and document the reason in a brief inline comment near the override.
- Before shipping UI changes to a shared surface, verify parity in both platforms by checking corresponding views and style tokens.
